tasks.prompt:
A long embedding backfill of real agent history died on a single Voyage timeout (an AbortError): the embedding client makes one attempt per batch, so one slow request kills the whole run.

Make embedDocuments (src/embeddings/voyage.ts) retry transient failures:
- timeouts and aborted requests, dropped connections, HTTP 429 and 5xx are retried with jittered exponential backoff, honouring a Retry-After header when there is one;
- at most VOYAGE_MAX_ATTEMPTS attempts in total (default 4), with base delay VOYAGE_BACKOFF_MS in milliseconds (default 1000; tests set it to 0);
- a 400 fails at once without a retry, and its error still reads voyage-http-400;
- after the last attempt, the last error is thrown.
Add tests.

Add a self-hosted reranker, so an operator can rerank with a model they serve themselves (an open-weights reranker behind vLLM or TEI) instead of a billed API.

New module src/search/rerank-http.ts exporting:
- class HttpReranker implementing the Reranker interface (src/search/reranker.ts), constructed with { url, model?, key?, queryTemplate?, docTemplate? } or null (not configured);
- it POSTs { model?, query, documents, top_n } to url (the Cohere/Jina shape vLLM serves), with query and each document wrapped by the templates when given ({query} and {doc} placeholders); text is scrubbed and truncated as the other rerankers do;
- readScores(reply): Map<number, number> reads { results: [{ index, relevance_score }] } (vLLM/Cohere), { data: [...] } (Voyage) and TEI's [{ index, score }]; anything else gives an empty map;
- toProbabilities(scores: number[]): number[] leaves a batch already within 0-1 alone and puts a batch with any score outside 0-1 (raw logits) through a sigmoid;
- results are blended with the retrieval score like the other rerankers and marked neural; on any failure, or when not configured, it returns the pool in retrieval order with neural: false.
Configuration from GATEWAY_RERANK_URL, GATEWAY_RERANK_MODEL, GATEWAY_RERANK_KEY, GATEWAY_RERANK_QUERY_TEMPLATE and GATEWAY_RERANK_DOC_TEMPLATE; selectable as the reranker "self-hosted". Add tests.
